@*
    Spec §6.9 "Pop out": the full /library page. Holds the Library at full width in
    LibraryExplorerLayout.SideBySide, StateKey "page" (its own remembered open file/divider,
    separate from the pane's "pane" key). Four query parameters, all optional: Root/Path open a
    specific file (the same pair LibraryPane.BuildPopOutUri builds); ScopeRoot/ScopePath, when
    BOTH are given, scope the whole page to that folder exactly like a scoped explorer elsewhere
    (Spec §6.16) - a single, not the pair, leaves the page unscoped. When the Library is disabled
    the page shows the settled refusal instead of ever constructing an explorer.

    ShowScopeRoot is false exactly when scoped: the only producer of ScopeRoot/ScopePath today is
    LibraryNavLink.razor's own sidebar rows, each already highlighted/selected while this page is
    open, so neither the title above the tree nor a folder row that exists only to be expanded
    (Spec §6.16's scope top node) earns its place - LibraryTree flattens straight to that root's own
    children instead. Unscoped (the whole Library, every root), ShowScopeRoot stays true since names
    are the only way to tell those roots apart. LibraryPane.razor makes the identical call for its
    own per-root sidebar rows, for the identical reason.

    <LibraryExplorer /> carries @key="this.QueryKey()": a same-page navigation (the sidebar's own
    per-root rows, LibraryNavLink.razor, each linking here with a different ?scopeRoot=) changes
    only this routable page's query parameters, so the Router reuses the existing page instance and
    calls SetParametersAsync again rather than remounting it - LibraryExplorer's own Scopes are only
    ever resolved once, from OnInitialized, so without this key a second root's link would update
    Scopes but go on showing the first root's already-resolved tree. The key doubles as the fix: a
    differing query also tears down and remounts LibraryExplorer, so it resolves the new Scopes/
    InitialFile fresh (LibraryPaneHost.razor keys LibraryPane on State.Scope for the identical
    reason).

    Named "Library" in Agency.Huddle.App.Components.Pages: distinct from the Agency.Huddle.App.Library
    namespace (no type there is named Library), so no @namespace override is needed - only fully
    qualifying is ever ambiguous, and this file never needs to.
*@
@page "/library"
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Library
@inject IOptions<TeamOptions> Options

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.False" Class="pa-4">
    @if (!this.Enabled)
    {
        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Info" role="status" Class="library-disabled-alert">The Library is turned off.</MudAlert>
    }
    else
    {
        <LibraryExplorer @key="@this.QueryKey()" Layout="LibraryExplorerLayout.SideBySide" StateKey="page"
                          Scopes="@this.Scopes()" ShowScopeRoot="@(this.Scopes() is null)" InitialFile="@this.InitialFile()" />
    }
</MudContainer>

@code {
    private bool Enabled => this.Options.Value.Library.Enabled;

    /// <summary>The pinned root id of the file to open, from <c>?root=</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public string? Root { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The file's path relative to <see cref="Root"/>, from <c>?path=</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter, SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public string? Path { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The scope's root id, from <c>?scopeRoot=</c>. Only takes effect together with <see cref="ScopePath"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter, SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public string? ScopeRoot { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The scope's path relative to <see cref="ScopeRoot"/>, from <c>?scopePath=</c>. Only takes effect together with <see cref="ScopeRoot"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter, SupplyParameterFromQuery]
    public string? ScopePath { get; set; }

    private IReadOnlyList<LibraryLocation>? Scopes() =>
        this.ScopeRoot is not null && this.ScopePath is not null
            ? [new LibraryLocation(this.ScopeRoot, this.ScopePath)]
            : null;

    private string? InitialFile() => this.Root is not null && this.Path is not null ? this.Path : null;

    /// <summary>Every query parameter that changes what <see cref="LibraryExplorer"/> shows, joined so a differing value forces the <c>@key</c> remount described above.</summary>
    private string QueryKey() => string.Create(
        System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture,
        $"{this.Root}|{this.Path}|{this.ScopeRoot}|{this.ScopePath}");
}
